; Account-scoped `check`/`assert` sub-directives and `= expr` automated
; transactions run their expressions through one evaluator.  Both must
; see the primary date while --effective is in force (the #2945 rule),
; and both report a failed check with the transaction's position and the
; check's own position.

account Expenses:Food
    assert aux_date != date
    check amount < $50

= expr "account =~ /^Expenses:Food$/"
    assert aux_date != date
    check amount < $40

2024/01/05=2024/02/01 * Grocer
    Expenses:Food                $60.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg --effective
24-Feb-01 Grocer                Expenses:Food                $60.00       $60.00
                                Assets:Cash                 $-60.00            0
__ERROR__
Warning: "$FILE", line 15: Transaction check failed: (amount < {$40.00})
  (check expression at "$FILE", line 11)
Warning: "$FILE", line 15: Transaction check failed: (amount < {$50.00})
  (check expression at "$FILE", line 7)
end test
